{% mcq answer="B" explanation="Atropine blocks muscarinic receptors competitively but has no effect on nicotinic actions. Muscle fasciculation and weakness are nicotinic effects, so they are not relieved by atropine. Bronchorrhoea, bradycardia and salivation are muscarinic." %}
