- A. Bronchorrhoea
- B. Muscle fasciculations and weakness
- C. Bradycardia
- D. Excessive salivation
{% /mcq %}

{% mcq answer="C" explanation="Neostigmine is a carbamate anticholinesterase. In carbamate poisoning the anionic site of the enzyme is not free for pralidoxime to attach to, so pralidoxime does not reactivate the enzyme and is considered contraindicated. It helps in organophosphate poisoning such as malathion, diazinon or sarin." %}
